<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernest II, Duke of Saxe-Gotha-Altenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1745–1804</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernest II was Duke of Saxe-Gotha-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altenburg">Altenburg</a> from 1772 and an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> ruler. A patron of science, he founded the Seeberg observatory near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a>, which became a leading centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-astronomy">astronomy</a> under Franz Xaver von Zach. He also supported education and the arts and was a member of the Illuminati.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernest-ii-duke-of-saxe-gotha-altenburg.jpg" alt="Ernest II, Duke of Saxe-Gotha-Altenburg" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Jonas Michael († 1791) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ernst-II_1775.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
